      "id": "TK-RX-001",
      "title": "Optimal radial engagement (ae) by material group for adaptive/trochoidal milling",
      "body": "Recommended radial width of cut as % of cutter diameter for adaptive clearing / trochoidal milling: Aluminum 6061: 25-40% (aggressive, good chip evacuation). Carbon Steel 1045: 15-25%. Alloy Steel 4140: 12-20%. Stainless 316: 10-18%. Titanium 6Al-4V: 8-15%. Inconel 718: 5-10%. Hardened Steel >50 HRC: 3-8%. Cast Iron: 20-30%. Copper/Brass: 25-40%. Start at the lower end for long tools (L/D > 4) or poor rigidity setups. These ranges maintain manageable cutting forces and heat generation while maximizing MRR.",
